      "sourceTextSha256": "b94e39045e152bf1e783e163243a1ad9b1fc25feeea4a5ec936a05ab2c95097c",
      "text": "Day 4 · An early start (07:00) for the 2.5-hour drive to Albina, on the border, and a pirogue across the Marowijne (Maroni) River to Saint-Laurent-du-Maroni, French Guiana, home of the Camp de la Transportation, the penal colony that operated from 1852 to 1953. Continue to Cayenne, the capital, with its colourful markets, historic landmarks and Creole cuisine, about 3.5 hours away, and end the day in Kourou. Make sure you have any required visa and a yellow fever vaccination certificate. (B)",
